  <h1>Policies</h1>

  <h2>Content disclaimer</h2>
  <p>All articles, headlines, and editorial content published in Imbryk Gazette are generated by artificial intelligence. They are fictional, speculative, and produced solely to demonstrate how different ideological lenses interpret world events. Nothing published here constitutes factual reporting, legal advice, financial advice, or the views of any real person or organisation.</p>

  <h2>User submissions</h2>
  <p>By submitting a news event or prompt you agree that your submission may be used to generate AI content on this platform. Do not submit personal data, confidential information, or content that infringes third-party rights. Submissions are subject to moderation and may be declined or modified.</p>

  <h2>Privacy</h2>
  <p>Imbryk collects only the information required to process your submission and payment. We do not sell your data to third parties. Payments are processed securely via Stripe — we do not store card details. For questions about your data, contact us at the address below.</p>

  <h2>Intellectual property</h2>
  <p>The Imbryk Gazette platform, its design, and its software are the property of Imbryk. AI-generated article text is produced dynamically and carries no copyright claim from Imbryk. You may share individual articles for non-commercial purposes with attribution.</p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>For policy enquiries, data requests, or takedown notices, please reach out via the submission portal or the contact details on the main Imbryk site.</p>
